<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Apitropos [Laws of Guardianship]</div>
<div class="halacha-ref">And in it will be explained the matter of Pesach.</div>

<div class="halacha-title">Halacha 3 &mdash; Part A (&sect;&sect;1&ndash;5)</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;1</div>

<p>Based on the Torah teaching on the statement of Rabbah bar bar Chanah: &ldquo;Akrukta&rdquo; &mdash; in siman 3. See there the entire teaching.</p>

<p>It is explained there regarding the matter of <span class="key-term">neginah</span> [melody/music]: that one who hears melody from a wicked musician &mdash; it is harmful to his service of the Creator. And conversely, when one hears melody from a proper and worthy musician, it is good for him. For the voice of the melody is drawn from the two birds &mdash; living, pure &mdash; which suckle from the place where the prophets suckle, which is the building of <span class="key-term">Malchus d&rsquo;kedushah</span> [the Kingship of holiness]. Therefore David was praised: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he knows how to play&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Shmuel I 16:18)</span> &mdash; for the melody is the building of the Kingship, and therefore he was fitting for the kingship. And this is what is written regarding him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;From following the nursing ewes He brought him, to shepherd&hellip;&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 78:71)</span>, etc.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the voice of the holy melody of a worthy musician. But when the musician is wicked, then he takes the voice of his melody from other birds that are in the klipah, which suckle from the breasts of the Malchus &mdash; and they are the mochin of Malchus d&rsquo;klipah [the Kingship of the husks]. <span class="verse">&ldquo;And when the night divides, then a herald proclaims&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;like the birds that are caught in the trap, so are the sons of men ensnared&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Koheles 9:12)</span>.</p>

<p>And the tikkun of the melody is through learning at night <span class="key-term">Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh</span> [the Oral Torah], which is Gemara, which is the aspect of night, etc. &mdash; see there. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Arise, sing out&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Aichah 2:19)</span> &mdash; that there should be an uplifting for the song &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;in the night&rdquo;</span> &mdash; through the aspect of night, which is the aspect of Sha&quot;S Talmud Bavli, as our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In darkness He has set me &mdash; this is the Talmud Bavli&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Sanhedrin 24a)</span>, etc. But when one studies not for its own sake, the study is not in its full worth. However, through studying at night, a thread of chesed is drawn upon him and protects him, so that he should merit to study for its own sake &mdash; see there.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;2</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Pesach and Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>. For then we merited song and melody of holiness, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The song shall be for you as on the night of the sanctification of the festival&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 30:29)</span>. And through this was the essential redemption. For we need to subdue the kingdom of wickedness, which is the kingdom of Pharaoh and Egypt, and to go out from there, and to elevate and raise up Malchus d&rsquo;kedushah, which is the kingdom of Israel &mdash; that they should not be subjugated under the hand of Pharaoh, which is the kingdom of wickedness. Rather, Israel should take the kingship and the dominion.</p>

<p>And this depends on the tikkun of the voice of the melody, as was explained above &mdash; that the essential building of the Kingship is through the voice of the melody. For Malchus d&rsquo;kedushah suckles from the two living, pure birds, which are the aspect of the voice of holy melody. And conversely, Malchus of wickedness of the Sitra Achra suckles from the two other birds that are in the klipah. Therefore the essential redemption was through the song and melody mentioned above. For through song and melody of holiness &mdash; that is, songs and praises to Hashem, blessed be He, with melody and song &mdash; through this, the kingdom of wickedness is subdued and Malchus d&rsquo;kedushah is elevated. This was the essential redemption, as above.</p>

<p>For the essential power of Pharaoh was from the voice and melody of the Sitra Achra. For Pharaoh is the letters of <span class="key-term">ha&rsquo;oref</span> [the back of the neck] &mdash; he suckled from behind the mouth, from the aspect of the severity of the judgments in the throat, as is brought in the Writings [of the Arizal]. That is, he suckled from the throat, from which the voice proceeds. For all voices proceed from the throat, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Call out with the throat&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 58:1)</span>. But Pharaoh suckled only from the judgments, from the aspect of the back &mdash; and from there is the hold of the wicked musician, from where the kingdom of wickedness suckles, which is the kingdom of Pharaoh. And therefore Pharaoh said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who is Hashem that I should listen to His voice?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Shemos 5:2)</span> &mdash; <span class="key-term">&ldquo;His voice&rdquo; specifically</span> &mdash; for he suckled from the voice of the Sitra Achra, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;3</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">prohibition of chametz and the mitzvah of eating matzah</span>. For the distinction between chametz and matzah is only that chametz rises through leavening, while matzah is baked immediately when water is placed on the dough, and one does not allow it to rise through leavening. That is, chametz &mdash; the air and the wind dominate it greatly through delaying it, through which it rises in leavening, which is through the air and the wind. But matzah is baked immediately, and one does not allow the air and the wind to dominate it so that it should rise in leavening.</p>

<p>For the air and the wind are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">kol</span> [voice], for all voices are through the air, as is known. And therefore now, on Pesach, at the time of Yetzias Mitzrayim, when we need to go out from the kingdom of wickedness &mdash; and the essential tikkun is through subduing the voice of the Sitra Achra and elevating the voice of holiness, as above &mdash; therefore it is forbidden for us now to eat chametz, G&ndash;d forbid. For we need to guard the dough from chametz, so that the air and wind of the world should not dominate there &mdash; the air from which proceed the voices that have not yet been purified from the contamination and defilement of Egypt.</p>

<p>For the redemption was not through our own efforts, but only through an <span class="key-term">is&rsquo;arusa d&rsquo;l&rsquo;aila</span> [an awakening from above], as is brought. For we had not yet received the Torah. And therefore now we need to guard the dough very carefully from the air of the world, which is not yet purified &mdash; from which comes the voice of the Sitra Achra &mdash; for this is the essential thing that we need to repair now, as above. Therefore we must be very careful about chametz, with &ldquo;it shall not be seen and it shall not be found,&rdquo; because there the air of the world that has not yet been purified takes the greatest hold &mdash; through which the dough becomes leavened, as above.</p>

<p>For the essential tikkun of the voice of the melody is through engaging in Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh at night, as is explained there. And now we have not yet received the Torah, and it is not in our hands to repair and purify the voice by ourselves. Rather, from Heaven He had compassion on us and caused us to hear the voice of holiness through Moshe Rabbainu &mdash; that is, all the prophecies that he prophesied to us in Egypt, from where comes the voice of holy melody, as above, through which was the redemption, as above. But since we have not yet received the Torah and have not yet merited by ourselves to purify and clarify the air in its completeness &mdash; from which come all the voices &mdash; therefore now we need to guard ourselves from chametz very much, because the air of the world that has not yet been purified has the greatest hold in it &mdash; and through this the dough becomes leavened, as above.</p>

<p>Rather, we must eat matzah, which we guard very carefully so that the air of the world should not dominate it. Rather, immediately when water comes upon the dough, we bake it right away. And through this, that we guard the matzah and do not allow the air of the world to dominate it, through this we flee completely from the air of this world, where the voice of the Sitra Achra takes hold. Rather, we merit the voice of holy melody &mdash; which is song and Hallel, melody and song to Hashem, blessed be He &mdash; through which was the essential redemption, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The song shall be for you as on the night of the sanctification of the festival,&rdquo;</span> as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;4</div>

<p>And this is why the matzah is called <span class="key-term">lechem oni</span> [bread of affliction/answering] &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;that we answer upon it many things,&rdquo;</span> as our Sages of blessed memory said. That is, holy voices that we answer upon the matzah on Pesach. For because we guard it from the air of this world, where the voices of the Sitra Achra take hold, through this we merit to answer upon it many things &mdash; that is, holy voices &mdash; the aspect of Hallel and holy melody. For when this one falls, the other rises, as above.</p>

<p>For now, on Pesach, is the beginning of Israel&rsquo;s drawing close to their Father in Heaven. And the essential drawing close and cleaving of the Jew to Hashem, blessed be He, is through the voice of holy melody, as is known &mdash; the great virtue of melody for whoever wants to cleave himself to Hashem, blessed be He. For melody has a great power to draw a person to Hashem, blessed be He. And therefore, in the future, when there will be the essential drawing close and cleaving to Hashem, blessed be He &mdash; which will be the essential reward &mdash; then song and melody will be aroused in the world, as it is taught in the Zohar, and as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Come, gaze from the peak of Amanah&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Shir HaShirim 4:8)</span>. And as is explained in many verses &mdash; that the essential drawing close and cleaving is through the voice of melody. And as is understood from the words of our master, our teacher, and our rabbi, of blessed memory, in many places, and in particular in the Tale of the Seven Beggars &mdash; of the third day, and the fourth day, and the sixth day &mdash; of the great and overwhelming virtue of melody. And as is explained further in his holy conversations.</p>

<p>Therefore now, on Pesach, when we need to draw close to Hashem, blessed be He, therefore we need to repair the voice of the melody and to guard ourselves from the voice of the melody of the Sitra Achra. Therefore we must be careful about chametz and eat matzah, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;5</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Pesach, matzah, and maror</span>. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">mitzvah of telling the story of Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Pesach &mdash; peh sach</span> [&ldquo;the mouth speaks&rdquo;]. For this is the essential thing: to speak of all His wonders and to tell at length about this, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And whoever tells at length about Yetzias Mitzrayim &mdash; behold, this is praiseworthy.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>For the voice of the melody is very, very precious and has a great power to arouse a person &mdash; that is, to arouse the minds, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The voice arouses the kavanah&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Berachos 24b)</span>. But the essential completeness of the voice is when one connects it to the dibbur [speech] with a firm and strong connection. For this is the essential aspect of the totality of all the yichudim [unifications] &mdash; to unify and connect the voice with the speech, as is understood from the holy Zohar and from the words of our master, our teacher, and our rabbi, of blessed memory, in the Torah teaching &ldquo;Sason v&rsquo;simchah yimatzai vah&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(siman 178)</span>.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of needing to connect and bind the da&rsquo;as to the heart, which is the essential completeness of the true da&rsquo;as, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall know today and bring it to your heart&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 4:39)</span>, as our master, our teacher, and our rabbi, of blessed memory, wrote elsewhere. For the voice, which is the aspect of mochin &mdash; for the voice impacts the mind, in the aspect of: &ldquo;The voice arouses the kavanah&rdquo; &mdash; its essential completeness is when it is drawn into the heart, until one&rsquo;s heart is warmed through it with an enthusiasm of holiness, until one merits holy words, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;My heart was hot within me; in my meditation a fire burned; I spoke with my tongue&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 39:4)</span>.</p>

<p>For the voice, even though it is very precious &mdash; for through it is the essential cleaving and drawing to Hashem, blessed be He, as above &mdash; nevertheless, as long as the voice is not unified with the speech, the Sitra Achra still has a hold. For their essential hold is from the world of separation &mdash; from the aspect of the voice that is distant from the speech &mdash; from where the nations of the world and the wicked have their hold. Their hold is from the aspect of the voice of melody of the Sitra Achra &mdash; that is, from wicked musicians who have the power to draw a person, G&ndash;d forbid, to the vanities of this world and their desires.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of Pharaoh, who is the letters of ha&rsquo;oref &mdash; whose suckling was from the throat, from which the voice proceeds, as above. And it is taught in the kavanos: <span class="verse">&ldquo;We were slaves to Pharaoh in Egypt&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of Pharaoh wanting to hold back the minds in the narrows of the throat, and not allow them to spread and be revealed outward. For from there was his suckling &mdash; as long as the minds are sealed above in the narrows of the throat, he suckles from there. And through this, Israel below are also subjugated under him.</p>

<p>And the essential Yetzias Mitzrayim is the aspect of the minds spreading and being revealed and going out from the narrows of the throat, etc. &mdash; see there. That is, the root of the voice, which is the aspect of mochin, is from a very high and exalted place &mdash; from the aspect of the sparkling of G&ndash;dliness that sparkles within each person&rsquo;s mind. For Hashem, blessed be He, in His mercy, contracts Himself through many contractions to illuminate within each person&rsquo;s mind a sparkling of G&ndash;dliness. And through this He hints to him and calls him to be drawn after Him. And this sparkling is the aspect of voices that come from above to call a person to be drawn after Him, blessed be He. And all voices are drawn from there. And therefore the voice has a great power to draw a person to Him, blessed be He &mdash; because it is drawn in its root from a high place, from the aspect of the sparkling of G&ndash;dliness. For the essential revelation of G&ndash;dliness is the aspect of voice, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The sound of words you hear, but you see no image &mdash; only a voice&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 4:12)</span>.</p>

<p>But Hashem, blessed be He, gave free will to man. And one who chooses life &mdash; when he hears this voice, which is the aspect of the herald that comes from above, he is drawn after it and sanctifies and purifies himself from all the desires of this world and its vanities. And then he merits to draw the voice, which is the aspect of the minds, into the heart, until he merits to receive holy words from above &mdash; that from the voice, combinations of letters and words should be formed, until he knows His will, blessed be He, and His mitzvos.</p>

<p>For even when one hears the aspect of a voice from above, one still does not know any mitzvah until one merits to sanctify and purify oneself so much that from the voice, speech is formed &mdash; until one merits that Hashem speaks with him and informs him of His Torah and His mitzvos. This is the aspect of the Avos of the world, who merited to hear His voice and to cleave to Him and to be drawn after Him, until they merited that Hashem, blessed be He, spoke with them and revealed to them many mitzvos. Until Moshe Rabbainu came, who merited this to the ultimate completeness &mdash; that he merited at all times through his good deeds to make from the voice, words, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he heard the Voice speaking to him from between the two keruvim&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bamidbar 7:89)</span>, etc. And through this he received all the words of this Torah and gave it to us.</p>

<p>But &ldquo;this opposite this&rdquo; [G&ndash;d made] &mdash; for Pharaoh and the like, when the aspect of a voice from above reached them, they did not want to cast off their evil deeds and be drawn after Him. And therefore they did not bind the voice, which is the aspect of the mind, to the heart, and did not make from the voice, words. On the contrary, they diverted the voice and the da&rsquo;as to their evil ways. For <span class="verse">&ldquo;the ways of Hashem are straight &mdash; the righteous walk in them, and the transgressors stumble in them&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Hoshea 14:10)</span>. For because they do not want to cast off their evil deeds, they blemish the voice and the da&rsquo;as and divert the da&rsquo;as to their rationalizations, until they go astray and are perplexed into idolatry and heresy. And therefore even in idolatry and heresy, there are some sparks from the sparkling of His G&ndash;dliness, blessed be He, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In every place, incense is offered and presented to My Name&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Malachi 1:11)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;they call Him the G&ndash;d of gods.&rdquo; For even to them there reached some herald and sparkling from above, which is the aspect of a voice. But they corrupted it through their evil deeds, and through this they went astray to their evil ways.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of Pharaoh suckling from the narrows of the throat and wanting the minds to be held back and concealed there and not spread downward. For he did not want the voice to come into the speech, that Hashem, blessed be He, should reveal His will through the speech &mdash; which is the aspect of receiving the Torah. Rather, that the voice and the mind should be held back above, so that he could suckle from there, so that he would have the power to divert the voice and the da&rsquo;as as he wished, so that he could walk in the stubbornness of his evil heart.</p>

<p>And this is the totality of all the blemishes of all the philosophers and of those who are perplexed through wisdoms of vanity and strange opinions and evil counsel. And all of this is because when they are called to Hashem, blessed be He, through the voice and the herald that comes from above at all times &mdash; which are the stirrings of teshuvah and the arousal that comes upon a person every day &mdash; then they are not drawn after this voice and do not think of ways to repair their deeds. Rather, they follow their desires. And then many times the aspect of the voice becomes corrupted in them, until they divert the aspect of the voice, which is the da&rsquo;as, to their evil ways, and they say many rationalizations of vanity in a way that they walk in the stubbornness of their hearts and do not return to the true truth.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the exile of Egypt, which encompasses all the exiles &mdash; that is, that the voice and the minds are held back in the narrows of the throat, from where the Sitra Achra suckles, which diverts the words of the living G&ndash;d. And it does not allow the voice and the minds to spread and go out outward &mdash; that is, that His will, blessed be He, should be revealed in truth, so that we should know what to do and how to conduct ourselves in truth.</p>

<p>And therefore the essential tikkun of the voice is through the study of Gemara, which is Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh, as above. For Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh is the aspect of speech, the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Malchus &mdash; we call it &lsquo;the mouth&rsquo; and &lsquo;Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh.&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> For Torah shebichsav [the Written Torah] and Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh are the aspect of voice and speech, as is known. And one must bind them and unify them with a firm connection, for this is the essential aspect of the yichud &mdash; to unify and connect the voice and the speech, as above.</p>

<p>That is, Torah shebichsav is still in the aspect of voice, because from the Written Torah alone one still does not know any law clearly &mdash; how to conduct oneself in the mitzvos of the Torah. Therefore it is still in the aspect of voice, which is the root of the speech. Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh reveals to us all the detailed laws of the Torah, how to conduct oneself in every mitzvah &mdash; this is the essential speech, which reveals the will that is in the heart. For through the voice, one can call a person to oneself, but he still does not know what is wanted. But when he comes to him and speaks with him in words, then he knows his will.</p>

<p>And therefore, even though the root of the suckling of the Malchus is from the aspect of voice, as above, nevertheless the essential governance of the Malchus is through the speech, which reveals the will of the King &mdash; so that we may know what to do and with what we should serve Him and bring Him nachas ruach. This is the aspect of Torah sheb&rsquo;al peh, which is the aspect of speech, which explains and expounds the aspect of the voice, which is the aspect of Torah shebichsav, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the essential aspect of Yetzias Mitzrayim: that we merited through Moshe Rabbainu, who merited to bring the voice and the minds outward, until he revealed to us many mitzvos immediately at the time of Yetzias Mitzrayim, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;This month shall be for you,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Shemos 12:2)</span>. And afterward he gave us the Torah through this, as above.</p>

